-- check/bad (core): `sync` in an ordinary declaration's signature, which a
-- platform package may write (transparent-effects-proposal.md §15.2 item 1,
-- amended 2026-10-02). `program` never calls `view`, yet its summary says
-- `view` is `sync`, because the signature says so: `Main` hands it a
-- suspending function across the module boundary and is refused at the
-- field's value, and so is `Lib.page`, which hands its own parameter on.
-- `race` makes its marked parameter suspend itself, by joining it with a
-- suspending function, and is refused at the word.
pub foreign suspends get : Int -> String


pub program : { init : Int, view : sync (Int -> String) } -> Int
program p = p.init


pub race : sync (Int -> String), Bool -> String
race f fast = (if fast then f else get) 1
